  "notes": "A statically scheduled datapath: one time counter and a timetable of constant cycle numbers; every enable compares the counter with a constant, with no busy flag, valid bit or data-dependent control. Memory slices put one column of A and one row of B on operand streams per cycle, a multiply slice forms their outer product as exact 2W-bit products, a vector slice adds it into an AccW-bit accumulator, and C is written once, with done, at t = N + 3. Latency N + 4 (8 at N = 4). The flat product stream has 2*N*N*W bits, more than 2^31 when N*N*W >= 2^30.",
  "player": "quartzwren",
